+        // inner class's later method calls can still see its enclosing
+        // instance's `this` bindings (`bindThis` alone only covers real
+        // inheritance/mixin, not lexical outer-class nesting).
+        // A genuinely static class (top-level, or nested in an `object` --
+        // no outer instance pointer at the JVM level either) has no real
+        // lexically-enclosing `this` to capture at all: threading the full
+        // ambient env into it anyway (below) doesn't just do nothing, it
+        // actively leaks whatever unrelated `This` bindings happen to be
+        // live at ITS construction site (e.g. some other class's own
+        // ancestor-trait binding from a sibling computation) into this
+        // instance's outer/construction env, where `bindThis`'s "fill gaps
+        // only" fold then mistakes that leftover binding for this
+        // instance's own and never corrects it -- a real crash seen via
+        // `ArraySeq.ofRef` inheriting a stale `SeqOps.this` left over from
+        // an unrelated `List` computation. Only genuinely non-static
+        // (lexically instance-nested) classes get the ambient env.
+        val outerEnv = bindClassTypeParams(if fn.owner.isStatic then emptyEnv else withOuterInstance(env, fn.owner, newType), fn.owner, newType)
+        // An anonymous subclass (`new Dispatch[T] { ... }`, `Dispatch` an inner class of
+        // trait `SingleDispatch`): the enclosing instance its PARENT needs
+        // (`SingleDispatch.this`) is named by the parent constructor call's own prefix.
+        val outerEnvForParent =
+          if !fn.owner.isAnonymousClass then outerEnv
+          else
+            moduleSuperCtorCall(fn.owner) match
+              case Some(parentCall) =>
+                val callTree = parentCall match { case Block(_, e) => e; case other => other }
+                callTree match
+                  case Call(superFn, _) if superFn.symbol.isConstructor && !superFn.symbol.owner.isStatic =>
+                    superFn.filterSubTrees(_.isInstanceOf[New]).headOption match
+                      case Some(New(tpt)) => withOuterInstance(outerEnv, superFn.symbol.owner, tpt.tpe)
+                      case _ => outerEnv
+                  case _ => outerEnv
+              case None => outerEnv
+        val instance = if existing != null then existing else InterpretedInstance(fn.owner, outerEnvForParent)
+        // All clauses, not just the first: `rawArgs` (from `Call`'s
+        // extractor) is already flattened across every parameter clause,
+        // including trailing `(using ...)` ones, so the formal-param list
+        // must match that shape or later clauses get silently dropped by
+        // `bindNonErased`'s size-mismatch fallback.
+        val params = ddef.termParamss.flatten.map(_.symbol)
+        if debugEnabled then
+          Console.err.println(s"[interpretNew] params=$params ddef.rhs=${ddef.rhs.show}")
+        val bound = bindNonErased(params, rawArgs)
+        // Start from the *ambient* env (not `emptyEnv`) only for a genuinely
+        // non-static inner class (e.g. `ClassValueCompat`'s private
+        // `FallbackClassValue`), which needs its enclosing instance's
+        // `this` bindings threaded through to resolve an outer
+        // `self`/`ClassValueCompat.this`. A static class -- see `outerEnv`
+        // above -- gets a fresh env instead, so its own constructor body
+        // can't see (and `bindThis`'s gap-filling fold can't be blocked by)
+        // whatever unrelated bindings happened to be ambient at its call site.
+        val withParams = bindThis(bound.foldLeft(outerEnvForParent)((e, pv) => e.updated(pv._1, pv._2)), fn.owner, instance)
+        if !ddef.rhs.isEmpty then
+          ddef.rhs match
+            // Class-body `val`s (private state the class keeps across later
+            // method calls, e.g. a derivation macro's memoization maps) get
+            // captured into `instance.fields` as they're bound -- see
+            // `interpretBlock`.
+            case Block(stats, expr) => interpretBlock(stats, expr, fn.owner, instance.fields)(using withParams)
+            case other => interpretTree(other)(using withParams) // else: trivial constructor, nothing to run
+        // NOTE: a fix was attempted here for a superclass constructor call
+        // carrying its own real arguments (e.g. `new Eval.Defer[A](() =>
+        // a) {}`, whose `thunk` field's real value lives in the PARENT
+        // constructor call, in `Template.parents` -- `-Yretain-trees`
+        // doesn't put it in THIS class's own primary constructor body at
+        // all). It had to be reverted: searching every constructed
+        // object's enclosing top-level unit for a matching superclass call
+        // (`localSuperCtorCall`, since removed) turned out to run for far
+        // more constructions than intended -- essentially any `new
+        // SomeClass(...)` where `SomeClass` extends anything with its own
+        // constructor args, which is most of them -- and broke unrelated,
+        // previously-working macro derivations (observed: upickle's own
+        // `ReadWriter` derivation regressed to "Unexpected tree could not
+        // be interpreted: This(Ident(Exclusive))"). Left as a known gap
+        // rather than re-attempted broadly.
+        // Common case: a case class's constructor params double as fields.
+        bound.foreach((p, v) => instance.fields.getOrElseUpdate(p.name.toString, v))
+        // `new Foo(args) { ... }` (anonymous-subclass instantiation, e.g.
+        // cats' own `Eval.defer`: `new Eval.Defer[A](() => a) {}`): desugars
+        // to a synthetic `$anon` class whose OWN primary constructor takes
+        // NO value params at all -- the real args (`() => a`, meant for
+        // `Defer`'s `thunk` field) live in the SUPERCLASS constructor call
+        // instead, in `$anon`'s own `Template.parents` (`-Yretain-trees`
+        // never puts them in `$anon`'s own trivial ctor body -- same gap
+        // `moduleSuperCtorCall` above works around for `object Foo extends
+        // Bar(args)`, reused here for a `$anon` class instead of a module
+        // class). Narrowly scoped to anonymous classes ONLY: a plain named
+        // class always has its own real ctor body already handling this
+        // correctly via `bound` above. A previous, broader attempt here (for
+        // *every* `new SomeClass(args)`, not just anonymous ones) regressed
+        // unrelated, already-working derivations (upickle's `ReadWriter`,
+        // see the reverted-fix note above) and was reverted; restricting to
+        // `isAnonymousClass` can't touch those, since a named class's
+        // instantiation never reaches this branch at all.
+        // Also a NAMED class with a superclass (anywhere up its superclass
+        // chain) exposing constructor-param fields (`class TransformerMacros(q:
+        // Quotes) extends PlatformBridge(q)`, `class PlatformBridge(q) extends
+        // MacroCommonsScala3(using q)`, `MacroCommonsScala3(using val quotes:
+        // Quotes)`): the ancestor's `quotes` accessor would otherwise read
+        // back `null`, as nothing ever runs the parent constructor calls.
+        // Gated on such a field actually existing (a plain parent whose ctor
+        // args are private/local is never read back, and is exactly the broad
+        // case that regressed upickle, see above), and `getOrElseUpdate`
+        // below never overrides a field already bound.
+        val ancestorExposesParamFields =
+          !fn.owner.isAnonymousClass && fn.owner.isClass &&
+            fn.owner.asClass.baseClasses.tail.exists { ps =>
+              ps.isClass && !ps.is(Trait) && !ps.is(JavaDefined) && ps != defn.ObjectClass && ps != defn.AnyClass &&
+                // `evidence$N` (a context bound's `ClassTag`/`Type`, e.g.
+                // hearth's `MacroExtension[Macro: ClassTag]`) is private too,
+                // but later read back by the parent's own methods.
+                ps.asClass.paramAccessors.exists(a => a.isTerm && a.is(ParamAccessor) && (!a.isAllOf(PrivateLocal) || a.name.toString.startsWith("evidence$")))
