+   *  entry kind, never as a flattened literal string, so `rootTreeContaining`
+   *  called with the *displayed* name (`sym.name.toString`, which DOES
+   *  include the `inline$`/`$default$N`/etc decoration) always misses --
+   *  `mightContain` binary-searches an array of only-ever-`SimpleName`
